Z||000002||Fierowrecker||04-11-2001||10:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 85seNUT:<BR><B>If i can manage to get my hands on 16's or even 17's would i have to upgrade my brakes?  or anything else?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I would get those cross drilled rotor plates that hide the real brake rotors and calipers...<BR>Why?<BR>To reduce the brake dust!!!<BR>If the overall size of the tire remains the same, there should be no difference in brake performance...<BR>Although, you will have the room to install bigger rotors and calipers!!!<BR>But if you do that, you might not want the rotor plates, as you might want to show them off!!!<BR>crash...||||reg||1
